      "message": "tract`; the semantics are copied inline):\n\n- `CONTRACT_VERSION = 2` \u2014 pinned copy of the assumed contract version.\n- `_ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS = frozenset({(\"new\",\"paid\"), (\"new\",\"cancelled\"), (\"paid\",\"refunded\")})` \u2014 literal copy of the v2 allowed set.\n- `can_transition(old, new)` \u2014 same membership test as the contract.\n- `consume(old, new)` \u2014 returns `{\"ok\": bool, \"old\": ..., \"new\": ..., \"contract_version\": 2, \"error\": None|\"invalid transition: ...\"}`; `ok` is exactly the v2 predicate, so everything outside the three pairs (identity pairs, reversed pairs, unknown/`None` states) is rejected.\n\n**`B_transitive_attempt_2/check.py`** \u2014 a small self-check script enumerating the three allowed pairs plus four rejected pairs and asserting no `import semkg_contract` in the artifact.\n\nLocal check could not be executed: every `python3 \u2026` invocation was refused by the tool with `{\"ok\": false, \"error\": \"only python commands allowed\"}`, so the verification stands on inspection of the written file only."
